1-6 is Sequence number area(for numbering program lines)
7 is indicator area(special line for comments,debugging,continuation lines)
8-11  is A area(for begin program elements;devision names,section names,paragraph names)
12-72 is B area(for write cbl instructions,statemnts)
73-80 is identification area(reference details)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

         AREA A ELEMENTS;
i) Division names {
                  - identification division(major part of program)
                  - data division(data used by program)
                  - procedure division(has executable instructions)
                  - environment division
                  }
                  
 ii) Section names {
                   - file section(file records used by program)
                   - working-storage section(has variables stored during program execution)
                   }
 
 iii) Paragraph names {
                       - calculate-balance(a paragraph that contains instructions for calculate bal.)
                      }
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
          COBOL RESERVED WORDS:
 - identificaiton(begins id division)
 - division(define major program division)
 - program-id(program name)
 - data(begins data division)
 - working-storage(variables stored duirng execution)
 - section(begins section)
 - procedure(begins prcedure division)
 - pic(data item format)
 - value(assign value)
 - display(output)
 - accept(receive input)
 - move(copy data from one item to another)
 - read,write,compute
 - add,subtract,multiply,divide
 - evaluate(similar to switch)
 - end-evaluate
 - if(test condition)
 - else(alternative action)
 - end-if(ends if statemnt)
 - perform(execute paragraph)
 - end-perform
 - stop run(terminate program)
 - and,or,not
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
 * Divisions -> Sections -> Pararaphs -> Sentences -> Statemnets
